# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ===== Unity YAML — the #1 source of pull conflicts on this project =====
# Two separate things are going on here, and both matter:
#
# 1. `-text` switches OFF the `* text=auto` normalization above. Unity always
#    writes LF; git on Windows was checking these back out as CRLF, so a
#    teammate who merely OPENED the project got a whole-file diff on every
#    scene. Two people with whole-file diffs = a guaranteed conflict on pull,
#    even when nobody edited the same object.
#
# 2. `merge=unityyamlmerge` routes conflicts through Unity's own YAML merge
#    tool, which understands objects and components instead of raw lines.
#    Line-based merging of a .unity file produces YAML that still "merges"
#    but loads as a corrupt scene — worse than an honest conflict.
#    Each dev enables the driver once; see TEAM_SETUP.md. Without it git
#    just falls back to the normal merge, i.e. no worse than before.
*.unity      -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.prefab     -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.asset      -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.mat        -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.anim       -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.controller -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.overrideController -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.physicMaterial2D   -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.playable   -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.mask       -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.terrainlayer -text merge=unityyamlmerge
*.spriteatlas  -text merge=unityyamlmerge

# .meta files are small and merge fine line-by-line, but they must not be
# EOL-normalized either — a rewritten .meta detaches a GUID from its asset.
*.meta -text

# LDtk project/level/tileset files are machine-generated JSON. Never normalize;
# regenerate from Tools/MapPipeline instead of hand-merging a conflict.
*.ldtk  -text
*.ldtkl -text
*.ldtkt -text

